### Streaming

- A function call part becomes a `tool_use` chunk. Vertex reports no call id of its own, so the function's name is used as the id as well ([validated by: yields tool_use chunks for function calls](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L76)).

parameters.new_string:
    required: ['score', 'feedback'],
  },
});
```

### Endpoint configuration

- `VertexConfig.apiEndpoint` is passed through to `new VertexAI({apiEndpoint})` when set, and omitted when absent so single-region deployments continue to derive their endpoint from `location` ([validated by: passes apiEndpoint to VertexAI when set and omits it when absent](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.acceptance.test.ts#L43)).
- An EU multi-region configuration (`{location: 'eu', apiEndpoint: 'aiplatform.eu.rep.googleapis.com'}`) reaches the Vertex SDK constructor without string rewriting and streams without logging the endpoint or prompt content ([validated by: routes an EU multi-region config end to end without rewriting location or logging apiEndpoint](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).

### Streaming

- A function call part becomes a `tool_use` chunk. Vertex reports no call id of its own, so the function's name is used as the id as well ([validated by: yields tool_use chunks for function calls](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L76)).
